MODIFIED. The OpenNGC data has been changed. It has been:
  * filtered to about 1,650 objects suitable for imaging (every Messier and
    Caldwell object, plus per-type magnitude and size cuts);
  * given a derived V-band mean surface brightness for each object, computed
    from OpenNGC's magnitudes, sizes and (for galaxies) HyperLEDA mean surface
    brightness, with typical values standing in where no usable magnitude
    exists. A nebula's magnitude that is a star's or a cluster's, or is
    shared by several entries, is not used, and not shown;
  * corrected in places (object sizes, positions, types, a few magnitudes,
    merged duplicate entries), and each correction is listed with its reason
    in scripts/build_catalog.py;
  * given extra common names and aliases (names.csv), and duplicate rows
    turned into aliases of their master entries.

